  "text": "Recipe: Air-Fried Pasta Chips\nCreator: Padma Subramanian\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: brown rice quinoa pasta, red lentil pasta, coriander powder, turmeric powder, red chilly powder, garam masala powder, kasuri methi, salt, oregano, garlic powder\nCooking methods: boil, air-fry\nInstructions: (1) Buy a pack of Whole Food Plant-Based compliant pasta. I took some brown rice quinoa pasta and some red lentil pasta.\n(2) Cook it al dente. Drain thoroughly.\n(3) Take a bowl. Add coriander powder, turmeric powder, red chilly powder, garam masala powder, kasuri methi and salt (optional). Add half the pasta and mix thoroughly.\n(4) Pre heat the air fryer at 400F and arrange in single layer. Cook till crispy, shaking it at intervals to prevent burning. It took me about 10 to 12 mins.\nTake some dry oregano, garlic powder and salt. Mix well with the rest half cooked pasta and air fry the same way.\n(5) The pasta turned out absolutely crispy like chips :)\nNotes: CHAKLI & MATHRI",
